@startuml DevPorts
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: discover a workspace's run commands, match each to the port it serves, and offer to publish them from an sbx sandbox
' covers: internal/devports/**, internal/run/choices.go (portsRow, appsRow, selectedPorts, addonHeading), internal/run/run.go (rememberedPorts, portsToRemember, planPorts)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (PlanPorts, portPublish, ReportPorts, DevServerScript, StartDevServers), internal/agentsettings/agentsettings.go (Workspaces, PortsFor, RememberPorts)
' covers: internal/devports/android.go, packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_android_install, _proveo_debug_apk, PROVEO_TOOLCHAIN_READY)
' covers: internal/run/ports_row_test.go, internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox_test.go, e2e/ports_publish_test.go
' covers: internal/devports/hostport.go (HostPorts, HostPortFor, HostPortWhy), internal/devports/hostport_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go (More.Off, toggleMore, moreHelp, drawMore, Selections), internal/choiceui/more_off_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/android_install_lib_test.go, e2e/android_seed_install_test.go
'   the form this row joins ......... _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   the publish half it generalises . _spec/_plans/tools-and-localhost-tunnels.puml (cdpPublish was the only caller)
'   the stream that reports it ...... _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml
'
' ── A STATIC CATALOG, NOT A PROBE ──────────────────────────────────────────
' proveo never runs the project to learn its port. It reads the files that
' NAME the run command and matches each line against a closed catalog:
'   package.json scripts .... dev · start · serve · preview · storybook · develop · dev:*
'   mise.toml [tasks.X] ..... same names, the run = line
'   Makefile targets ........ same names, the recipe lines
'   Procfile(.dev) .......... every process line
'   manage.py ............... django runserver :8000
'   main.go ................. ListenAndServe(":N") and friends — explicit only
' An explicit port in the line (--port N, -p N, PORT=N, --bind h:N,
' runserver h:N) beats the tool's default. `go run` and `cargo run` have no
' default, so they appear only with an explicit port.
'
' ── ONE CANDIDATE PER PORT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A monorepo names the same port many times (next dev and next start both
' :3000). Dedupe keeps one per port: explicit over default, then the file
' nearest the root. The walk stops at depth 2 and skips dependency trees and
' dot-dirs, so node_modules never offers a port.
'
' ── THE ROW: OFFERED, NEVER PRE-TICKED ─────────────────────────────────────
' The execution divider's row is now labelled "OS" (heading stays
' "execution"). "ports" sits under it only when docker (sandbox) is the
' runtime: the docker+egress backend published nothing (and is deleted since
' 2026-10-16, so sbx is always the runtime). Every box starts
' unticked — publishing opens an inbound path, and the closed default the
' tunnels plan argues for is kept. Several ports tick independently.
' Four ports fill the four columns. A fifth replaces column 4 with
' ""...More""; the cell opens a dropdown of the rest, each a checkbox.
' Space ticks the highlighted row. ↑↓ moves inside the list until an
' edge, then the form. The cell shows [x] while any hidden port is on.
'
' ── PUBLISH: A DIGIT 1–9 PREPENDED TO THE HOST PORT (2026-10-22) ──────────
' DECISION SOURCE (user, 2026-10-22): "Whenever offering to publish ports in
' internal/choiceui/, always prepend the host's port with a number, from 1-9
' only. Start by checking <port>:1<port>, e.g. the sbx (sandbox) port 8083 and
' the host's 18083 — check if 18083 is available on the host, and raise the
' prefix up to 9; disable the selection otherwise."
' Supersedes "HOST = GUEST when free, else a random free loopback port".
'   HostPorts(G) .... k·10^digits(G) + G for k = 1…9, kept while ≤ 65535
'                     8083 → 18083 … 58083 (68083+ overflow)
'                     18083 → none: every 5-digit G overflows
'                     never G itself, never prefix 0
'   HostPortFor ..... the first HostPorts entry the probe accepts
'   probe ........... sandbox.LoopbackFree: net.Listen on 127.0.0.1:H.
'                     `sbx ports --help` (v0.49.2): no HOST_IP + no PROTOCOL
'                     → tcp4 bound on 127.0.0.1, so the probe tests the
'                     interface sbx binds.
' THE ROW: portsRow(found, chosen, free) runs HostPortFor per candidate. The
' help names "host 127.0.0.1:H". No H → Row.Off + Row.OffWhy = HostPortWhy:
' "host :18083 … :58083 are all in use" or "no host port 1G…9G fits under
' 65535"; the box never starts ticked, even when remembered. A port folded
' behind ...More uses More.Off (parallel to More.On) with the same Row.OffWhy:
' space refuses it, the dropdown paints it warn, the help adds "off: …",
' Selections skips it. The ...More cell itself stays on, so the list opens.
' PUBLISH: planPorts re-runs the same HostPortFor at launch, so the -p entry
' equals what the help showed unless the host bound H in between; then the
' next prefix wins and ReportPorts says "host :<first> was taken". A ticked
' port with no H (a --yes run on a remembered 5-digit port, or every prefix
' taken by launch) is dropped with a warning naming HostPortWhy. PlanPorts
' also keeps two guests off one host port.
' Each kept port becomes `sbx run -p H:G` after the CDP relay's entry.
' RELAY PORT RESERVED (2026-10-22): the CDP relay's host port comes from
' FreeLoopbackPort (bound then released) before planPorts probes, so a free-
' looking prefixed H could equal it. DECISION SOURCE (user, 2026-10-22):
' "Exclude it from planning". planPorts(…, relay) passes cdpPort to
' PlanPorts(ports, free, reserved...) as already taken, so the candidate is
' skipped for the next prefix. Gap closed. Pinned by
' TestPlanPortsSkipsTheBrowserRelayHostPortForTheNextPrefix.
'
' ── THE RUN COMMAND RUNS IN THE SANDBOX (2026-10-05) ───────────────────────
' Publishing an empty port is pointless, so proveo starts the server itself:
' devports.Launch turns the candidate into `HOST=0.0.0.0 PORT=N <cmd>` run in
' the source's directory under the agent workdir —
'   package.json .. <npm|pnpm|yarn|bun> run X (+ the tool's bind args)
'   mise.toml ..... mise run X -- <bind>     Makefile .. make X
'   Procfile ...... the line (+ bind)        manage.py . runserver 0.0.0.0:N
'   main.go ....... go run .
' The lockfile nearest the source picks the package manager. A line that
' already binds 0.0.0.0 gets no extra args. StartDevServers runs it through
' `sbx exec … bash -lc`, skips when the port already answers (the agent may
' have started it), logs to /tmp/proveo-dev-N.log, and restarts it with
' 3 s → 30 s backoff while the sandbox runs — deps installing in a fresh
' clone make the first attempts fail.
'
' ── A CLONE'S SERVER WAITS FOR THE CLONE (2026-10-20) ──────────────────────
' MEASURED: TestPortsPublishE2E failed "GET http://127.0.0.1:4310/PORTS_OK
' never reached the server proveo started" on a clone-mode run.
' StartDevServers' goroutines start before `sbx run` and fire once
' sbx.Running; sbx clones only into an EMPTY workspace that already exists
' (_spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml, "NOTHING MAY BE MOUNTED").
' [Inference] The exec could `cd` into that empty dir, or into one the clone
' later replaced, and start python there; the exec then blocks for as long as
' python runs, so the loop never restarts it in the real checkout.
' FIX: DevServerScript(workdir, clone, p). When in.Clone, the script polls
'   until git -C <workdir> rev-parse -q --verify HEAD && [ -n "$(ls -A <workdir>)" ]
' once a second for devRetryMax (30 s), then exits 1 into the existing
' backoff; the 30 s attempt resets the delay to devRetryMin. The emptiness
' half exists because rev-parse alone passes in an empty dir nested inside a
' parent repository. A worktree clone passes
' once the seed's `git worktree add` lands. A mounted checkout (in.Clone
' false) skips the gate, so a non-git mount still starts at once.
' Pinned by TestDevServerScriptWaitsForTheCloneBeforeItStartsTheServer (the
' rendered script) and TestDevServerScriptCloneGateRunsOnlyOnceTheCloneLands
' (the gate run by bash: an empty dir fails, a committed repo passes).
' e2e: assertServed's 2-minute GET deadline now starts once sbx.Running names
' the workspace's claudecode sandbox (SandboxName of the path and of its
' realpath), at most 3 minutes after the port report: the report prints
' before `sbx run`, so boot and clone used to eat the server's window.
'
' ── REMEMBERED PER PATH, APPLIED ON EVERY RUN ──────────────────────────────
' agent-settings.yml gains `workspaces: {<real path>: {ports: [...]}}`,
' harness-independent: the ports belong to the project, not the agent. The
' answer seeds the row's ticks, and --yes / non-TTY runs publish it with no
' form. An answered "none" is kept as an empty list, so it is not re-asked
' as a first run. A remembered port no longer discovered is dropped with a
' warning. The answer is written only when the form DREW the ports row —
' a docker+egress run never showed it, so it never recorded "none".

' ── ANDROID APPS: THE SEED INSTALLS, THE HOST TRIGGERS (2026-10-05) ───────
' The same pattern for Android: a build file applying com.android.application
' (or the android.application alias) is an app module; applicationId, else
' namespace, is its package. The "apps" row sits beside "ports", sbx only,
' greyed until [x] android is ticked, unticked by default, remembered per
' path (workspaces.<path>.apps) and reused by --yes.
'   host   once the sandbox runs: `sbx exec … bash -lc` exports the adb
'          guest env, cd's to the agent workdir, sources /entrypoint-lib.sh
'          and calls proveo_android_install ":app|ca.proveo.hello" …
'   seed   proveo_android_install waits for PROVEO_TOOLCHAIN_READY — written
'          by proveo_seed after proveo_provision_toolchain, cleared at its
'          start — then per module:
'            build    ./gradlew (else gradle) <module>:assembleDebug
'            apk      _proveo_debug_apk: the first */debug/*.apk by path under
'                     <module dir>/build/outputs/apk, androidTest excluded;
'                     ":a:b" → a/b, "" → the build root
'            install  `adb install -r <apk>`
'            launch   `adb shell monkey -p <id> -c …LAUNCHER 1`
'          adb is the image's apt client (defs/base/Dockerfile); both calls set
'          ADB_SERVER_SOCKET=tcp:$ADB_HOST:$ADB_PORT from proveo_host_adb_env.
'          No adb client stops the run; a failed build, no APK or a failed
'          install skips the rest of that module and returns 1.
'          Log: /tmp/proveo-android-install.log (sandbox.AndroidLog).
'          AndroidApp.Task() names <module>:assembleDebug for the row's help
'          and ReportAndroidApps.
' WHY NOT installDebug (2026-10-20): TestAndroidAppInstallsFromTheSeed saw no
' ca.proveo.hello on the host emulator after `<module>:installDebug`.
' [Unverified] AGP's install task drives adb through its own client (ddmlib)
' and the SDK's platform-tools, which ensure_jvm_toolchain never installs
' (cmdline-tools only), and ddmlib likely ignores ADB_SERVER_SOCKET.
' The apt `adb` client honours ADB_SERVER_SOCKET, and the fixture's
' install.sh (assembleDebug + `adb install -r`) already took that path.
' On a failed install check the e2e prints this log from each sandbox it
' made (`sbx exec … cat`) and the host's `adb devices -l`.
' WHY THE HOST TRIGGERS: a re-attached sandbox keeps the env of its first
' launch (reuseOrCreate), so an env var could not carry this run's answer;
' `sbx exec` always carries it. Install + launch run ONCE; the agent re-runs
' assembleDebug + `adb install -r` after its own edits. The function ships
' in the image, so it reaches a sandbox after the harness image is rebuilt.

title Dev ports — a static catalog, an opt-in row, one -p per tick

component "Discover(root)\nwalk ≤ 2 levels\nskip deps + dot-dirs" as DISC <<app>>
component "catalog\nnext 3000 · vite 5173 · astro 4321\nng 4200 · storybook 6006 · django 8000\nflask 5000 · rails 3000 · hugo 1313 …" as CAT <<db>>
component "Match(line)\nexplicit port > tool default" as MATCH <<app>>
component "dedupe\none per port" as DEDUP <<app>>
component "portsRow\nunder execution · OS\nsbx only · unticked" as ROW <<app>>
component "PlanPorts\nfirst free 1G…9G ≤ 65535\nnot the relay port · none → dropped" as PLAN <<host>>
component "sbx run -p H:G" as SBX <<cloud>>
component "ReportPorts\nhttp://127.0.0.1:H → sandbox :G" as REP <<app>>
component "StartDevServers\nsbx exec bash -lc\nskip if served · clone: wait for HEAD · backoff" as DEV <<async>>
database "agent-settings.yml\nworkspaces.<path>.ports · .apps" as MEM <<db>>
component "appsRow\ngreyed until android\n:app ca.proveo.hello" as APPS <<app>>
component "proveo_android_install\nwait toolchain → assembleDebug\n→ adb install -r → monkey launch" as AINST <<async>>

DISC ARROW_MAIN MATCH : each run line
MATCH ARROW_MAIN CAT
MATCH ARROW_MAIN DEDUP
DEDUP ARROW_MAIN ROW : candidates
ROW ARROW_MAIN PLAN : ticked
PLAN ARROW_MAIN SBX
PLAN ARROW_MAIN REP
PLAN ARROW_MAIN DEV : Launch(cmd, dir)
MEM ARROW_MAIN ROW : seeds ticks · --yes uses as-is
ROW ARROW_OPTIONAL MEM : answered form
MEM ARROW_MAIN APPS
APPS ARROW_MAIN AINST : sbx exec, once
@enduml
